  "body": "Found by the read-only second read of PR #3307 (comment 7077842096). It is not confirmed by a run.\n\n## What the code does\nThe option \"write the stock as a Manual Guide i blank\" in `assets/posts/fanuc.cps` writes `G1902` or `G1900` before the first section. The guard at about line 602 refuses a WCS that is rotated about Z, and writes the comment `(NO BLANK BLOCK - <reason>)`.\n\n## The gap\nThe guard does not check a tilted (indexed) first setup. If the first section has a tilted work plane, the blank block can use the world axes. The simulation on the control can then show the blank in the wrong orientation. No comment tells the user.\n\nThe block is a blank definition for the simulation of the control. It is not a motion word. The option is off by default.\n\n## Necessary work\n1. Find if the stream lets a tilted first section reach the blank writer. Pin it with a test.\n2. If it does: refuse the blank for that case with a `(NO BLANK BLOCK - <reason>)` comment, as for the other cases.\n\nRefs #2769\n",
